{"absent":["Locking and concurrency rules for hypercalls and control regions","Full field enumeration beyond the truncated control list","Semantic effects and error reporting of version frequency CPU info and steal clock commands","Memory ordering and privilege requirements for block transfers","Caller obligations for result storage validity and alignment","Patch mechanism timing and true versus non true control selection"],"dossier":"D10","findings":[{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::VMWARE_HYPERVISOR_HB","arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::VMWARE_HYPERVISOR_OUT","arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::VMWARE_HYPERVISOR_PORT","arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::VMWARE_HYPERVISOR_PORT_HB","arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::VMWARE_HYPERVISOR_MAGIC"],"text":"Guest to host requests target IO port 0x5658. Two qualifier flags use low bit positions with high bandwidth at bit zero and output direction at bit one. The high bandwidth port value combines the base port with the high bandwidth flag. Every request carries unsigned authentication word 0x564D5868."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::VMWARE_CMD_GETVERSION","arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::VMWARE_CMD_GETHZ","arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::VMWARE_CMD_GETVCPU_INFO","arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::VMWARE_CMD_STEALCLOCK","arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::VMWARE_CMD_MASK"],"text":"Four command numbers are defined for version query at 10 and frequency query at 45 and virtual CPU information at 68 and steal clock at 91. A command mask of 0xf007f constrains valid command encodings."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::CPUID_VMWARE_FEATURES_ECX_VMMCALL","arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::CPUID_VMWARE_FEATURES_ECX_VMCALL","arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::VMWARE_TDX_VENDOR_LEAF","arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::VMWARE_TDX_HCALL_FUNC"],"text":"Two feature bits in the vendor feature word advertise trap support with VMMCALL at bit zero and VMCALL at bit one. Confidential guest interaction uses vendor leaf 0x1af7e4909 with function number 1."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::VMWARE_HYPERCALL"],"text":"The abstract hypercall operation has three machine encodings resolved by capability patching rather than by caller choice. The default uses a port based read while two alternate trap encodings apply when their respective processor features are present."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::vmware_hypercall1","arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::vmware_hypercall3","arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::vmware_hypercall4","arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::vmware_hypercall5","arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::vmware_hypercall6","arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::vmware_hypercall7"],"text":"A family of helpers exchanges a command word plus varying input words for a primary result word with optional extra 32 bit results through caller storage. Narrow forms carry one input and no extra outputs or one to two extra outputs while wide forms carry up to three extra inputs and up to four extra outputs. All forms return the primary hypervisor result directly."},{"kind":"state_machine","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::vmware_hypercall1","arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::vmware_hypercall3","arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::vmware_hypercall4","arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::vmware_hypercall5","arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::vmware_hypercall6","arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::vmware_hypercall7"],"text":"Each numbered helper selects among three dispatch modes by global state with fixed precedence. Confidential guest mode takes the confidential delegation path. Otherwise pre patch execution in non modular builds takes the slow delegation path. Patched execution uses the inline patched encoding. Argument values do not affect mode choice."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::vmware_hypercall_hb_out","arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::vmware_hypercall_hb_in","arch/x86/include/asm/vmware.h::VMW_BP_CONSTRAINT.